# The adjudication ledger is APPEND-ONLY. Union-merge it so concurrent appends (a guard-allowed PR
# append + the pushback cron's append) auto-combine instead of producing a rebase conflict that would
# wedge the sync (or, worse, leave conflict markers a direct push could ship). `union` is a git
# BUILT-IN driver (no custom command), so this cannot introduce a code-exec merge driver.
data/adjudications.jsonl merge=union

# Opt these two out of eol normalization. Both are machine-written and machine-read, never
# hand-edited, so there is no reason for git to rewrite their bytes on checkout. Today nothing
# in-tree byte-compares them - lib/verdictAnchor.ts:82 deliberately does NOT recompute
# chain_root, it only checks that the proof path matches, and chain_root is folded over
# canonical JSON rather than raw file bytes. So this is a guard against a future or external
# verifier that does hash the file as it sits on disk, which is the natural way to check an
# OpenTimestamps proof in public/anchors/<sha256>.ots against the artifact it commits to.
data/verdicts.json -text
data/verdict-anchors.json -text
